Z||000026||watts||11-27-2001||01:19 AM||||I don't want to throw cold water on his project, but...  I'm going to bet that when he got his bender and started to bend pipe, he found out how hard it is!<P>Hence whey my freind and I are building a hydraulic mandrel bender.  If you just try to bend pipe (especially stainless!) in a fairly tight radius, it'll crush waaaaay down in the center of the arc.<P>We're going to be building headers in mild steel and in stainless.  Complete stainless exhaust systems too.  These will be virtually bolt on's, with all spring hangers attached to the mufflers, and the pipes.  They'll have cats, downpipes, etc.<P>No pricing yet, but since we're in Canada, it'll be pretty good for you guys in the states.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||danny boy||11-27-2001||06:32 PM|||| Ok, here's the deal. All I have done so far is the catback system for my Stealth in 3" and a rear swaybar for the same.<BR> This isn't as easy as I thought, but my exaust didn't come out too bad. Hedders will be a different story. I'm having some personal problems at the moment so I really haven't had the time to mess with Fiero stuff yet.<BR>  Formula- I don't think we're moving. I think we're buying. My landlord died so I either have to move or buy, and tonight it was pretty much we're staying.||||reg||1
Z||000028||Joe Torma||11-28-2001||02:25 PM||||When I made hedders for my 3400...  It wasn't that difficult, the pipe was about $50 a length.  I used T409-bends nicely.  T304 you can polish...but this stuff is VERY expensive.<BR>I made a true dual system.<P>Joining all the pipes together is the worst part of the job.  I devised an easy way though.<BR>But hedders wouldn't be cheap if I was to sell them.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
